{"id":"y11-7-l3","label":"7 L3: Iteration and Trace Tables","steps":[{"id":"do-now","label":"Iteration Starter","type":"short-answer-validation","validatorId":"y11l3-do-now","validatorKey":"y11l3_do_now","content":"<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Iteration Starter</h2><p class=\"lesson-lead\">A quick recap of selection before today's new topic, iteration. Every ELSE branch in this chain contains another IF.</p><div class=\"lesson-do-now-columns\"><div><div class=\"lesson-code\"><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">IF Score &gt;= 70 THEN</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Grade &lt;- \"A\"</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">ELSE</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;IF Score &gt;= 60 THEN</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Grade &lt;- \"B\"</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;ELSE</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;IF Score &gt;= 50 THEN</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Grade &lt;- \"C\"</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;ELSE</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;IF Score &gt;= 40 THEN</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Grade &lt;- \"D\"</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;ELSE</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;IF Score &gt;= 30 THEN</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Grade &lt;- \"E\"</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;ELSE</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Grade &lt;- \"F\"</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;ENDIF</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;ENDIF</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;ENDIF</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;ENDIF</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">ENDIF</div></div></div><div class=\"lesson-exam-card\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-responses\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y11l3-do-now-a\">(a) Score = 68. State the value stored in <strong>Grade</strong>. [1]</label><input id=\"y11l3-do-now-a\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"do-now-a\" aria-label=\"Do Now part a\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y11l3-do-now-b\">(b) Score = 35. State the value stored in <strong>Grade</strong>. [1]</label><input id=\"y11l3-do-now-b\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"do-now-b\" aria-label=\"Do Now part b\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y11l3-do-now-c\">(c) Score = 15. State the value stored in <strong>Grade</strong>. [1]</label><input id=\"y11l3-do-now-c\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"do-now-c\" aria-label=\"Do Now part c\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-actions\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"donow-btn\" id=\"y11l3-do-now-check\">Check answers</button><strong>Total: 3 marks</strong></div><div id=\"y11l3-do-now-feedback\" class=\"pseudocode-feedback\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"></div><p class=\"exam-source\">Algorithm from Cambridge IGCSE 0478, May/June 2021 Paper 21, Question 4</p></div></div>"},{"id":"title","label":"Iteration and Trace Tables","content":"<div class=\"lesson-title-slide\"><p class=\"lesson-title-kicker\">Algorithms</p><h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Iteration and Trace Tables</h2><p>Year 11, Unit 7 L3</p></div>"},{"id":"teacher-talk-1","label":"Trace a Simple FOR Loop","type":"stepper","stepperId":"y11l3-stepper-1","stepperKey":"iteration_for_loop_basic","content":"<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Trace a Simple FOR Loop</h2><ul class=\"lesson-facts\"><li>FOR sets the loop variable to its starting value once, right at the start.</li><li>NEXT adds 1 to the loop variable and sends control back to the line after FOR.</li><li>The loop stops the moment the loop variable passes the end value.</li><li>A new trace table row still only appears when a variable changes or an output occurs.</li></ul><div id=\"y11l3-stepper-1\" class=\"lesson-stepper\"></div>"},{"id":"activity-1","label":"Trace a For Loop","type":"embedded-app","appId":"trace-table-practice","embedContainerId":"y11l3-embed-1","embedQuery":"view=walkthrough&idx=0&lang=cambridge","content":"<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Trace a For Loop</h2><p class=\"lesson-lead\">Predict how many times the loop will run, then press Step Forward once for each executed line. Notice that NEXT sends control back to the line after FOR, not back to FOR itself, and explain why the loop stops when it does.</p><div id=\"y11l3-embed-1\" class=\"lesson-embed\"></div>"},{"id":"teacher-talk-2","label":"Trace a Running Total","type":"stepper","stepperId":"y11l3-stepper-2","stepperKey":"iteration_for_loop_running_total","content":"<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Trace a Running Total</h2><ul class=\"lesson-facts\"><li>A running total (an accumulator) must be set to 0 before the loop begins.</li><li>Setting it inside the loop would reset it back to 0 on every pass instead of adding up.</li><li>Each pass adds the current value onto whatever the total already holds.</li><li>Instructions after the loop, like a final OUTPUT, only run once, after the loop finishes.</li></ul><div id=\"y11l3-stepper-2\" class=\"lesson-stepper\"></div>"},{"id":"activity-2","label":"Practice: For Loop Foundations","type":"embedded-app","appId":"trace-table-practice","embedContainerId":"y11l3-embed-2","embedQuery":"view=practice&lang=cambridge","embedView":"practice","algorithm":{"title":"For Loop Foundations","context":"The user ran the program and typed <strong>5</strong> when prompted for the bonus.","code":["bonus = int(input(\"Enter bonus:\"))","total = bonus","for i in range(1, 3):","    total = total + i","print(total)"],"cols":["Line","bonus","total","i","Output"],"answers":[{"Line":"1","bonus":"5","total":"","i":"","Output":""},{"Line":"2","bonus":"","total":"5","i":"","Output":""},{"Line":"3","bonus":"","total":"","i":"1","Output":""},{"Line":"4","bonus":"","total":"6","i":"","Output":""},{"Line":"3","bonus":"","total":"","i":"2","Output":""},{"Line":"4","bonus":"","total":"8","i":"","Output":""},{"Line":"5","bonus":"","total":"","i":"","Output":"8"}]},"content":"<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Practice: For Loop Foundations</h2><p class=\"lesson-lead\">Fill in the table below. Add a row only when a line changes a value or produces output, and keep track of every variable, not just the loop variable. Select Check Answers when ready.</p><div id=\"y11l3-embed-2\" class=\"lesson-embed\"></div>"},{"id":"formative","label":"Check Your Understanding","content":"<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Check Your Understanding</h2><p class=\"lesson-lead\">Questions to ask around the room:</p><ul class=\"lesson-facts\"><li>What three things does a FOR loop header need?</li><li>How many times does FOR Count &lt;- 1 TO 5 run?</li><li>Why must a running total be set to 0 before the loop starts, not inside it?</li><li>What exactly does NEXT do?</li></ul>"},{"id":"extension-iteration","label":"Extension: While and Do...Until Loops","type":"app-link","buttonId":"y11l3-extension-btn","appId":"trace-table-practice","content":"<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Extension: While and Do...Until Loops</h2><p class=\"lesson-lead\">Optional, for anyone who is already confident with FOR loops. A FOR loop is count-controlled, it always knows how many times it will run before it starts. A WHILE loop and a REPEAT...UNTIL loop are condition-controlled instead, they keep running until a condition changes, however many passes that takes.</p><div class=\"lesson-flow-task\"><h3>Key difference</h3><ul><li><strong>WHILE</strong> tests its condition before every pass, including the first. If the condition starts false, the loop body never runs at all.</li><li><strong>REPEAT...UNTIL</strong> tests its condition after every pass. The loop body always runs at least once, even if the condition is already true.</li></ul></div><div class=\"lesson-app-link\"><p>Open Trace Tables. Try the Walkthrough for While Loop, then Do...Until Loop, then try each on the Practice tab.</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"donow-btn\" id=\"y11l3-extension-btn\">Open Trace Tables</button></div>"},{"id":"plenary","label":"Plenary: Trace a Running Total","type":"short-answer-validation","validatorId":"y11l3-plenary","validatorKey":"y11l3_plenary","content":"<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Plenary: Trace a Running Total</h2><p class=\"lesson-lead\">Trace the FOR loop exactly as written. A new value only needs recording when it changes.</p><div class=\"lesson-do-now-columns\"><div><div class=\"lesson-code\"><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">1&nbsp;&nbsp;Total &lt;- 0</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">2&nbsp;&nbsp;FOR Number &lt;- 1 TO 4</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">3&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Total &lt;- Total + Number</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">4&nbsp;&nbsp;NEXT Number</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">5&nbsp;&nbsp;OUTPUT Total</div></div></div><div class=\"lesson-exam-card\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-responses\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y11l3-plenary-a\">(a) State the value of Total straight after the pass where Number = 2. [1]</label><input id=\"y11l3-plenary-a\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"plenary-a\" aria-label=\"Plenary part a\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y11l3-plenary-b\">(b) State the value of Total straight after the pass where Number = 4. [1]</label><input id=\"y11l3-plenary-b\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"plenary-b\" aria-label=\"Plenary part b\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y11l3-plenary-c\">(c) State the number of times line 3 executes. [1]</label><input id=\"y11l3-plenary-c\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"plenary-c\" aria-label=\"Plenary part c\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y11l3-plenary-d\">(d) State the output. [1]</label><input id=\"y11l3-plenary-d\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"plenary-d\" aria-label=\"Plenary part d\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-actions\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"donow-btn\" id=\"y11l3-plenary-check\">Check answers</button><strong>Total: 4 marks</strong></div><div id=\"y11l3-plenary-feedback\" class=\"pseudocode-feedback\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"></div><p class=\"exam-source\">Practice question in the Cambridge IGCSE 0478 exam style.</p></div></div>"},{"id":"plenary-2","label":"Plenary: Trace a FOR Loop Range","type":"short-answer-validation","validatorId":"y11l3-plenary-2","validatorKey":"y11l3_plenary_2","content":"<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Plenary: Trace a FOR Loop Range</h2><p class=\"lesson-lead\">A second FOR loop, this one starting above 1.</p><div class=\"lesson-do-now-columns\"><div><div class=\"lesson-code\"><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">1&nbsp;&nbsp;FOR X &lt;- 2 TO 5</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">2&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;OUTPUT X</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">3&nbsp;&nbsp;NEXT X</div></div></div><div class=\"lesson-exam-card\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-responses\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y11l3-plenary-2-a\">(a) State how many times the loop runs. [1]</label><input id=\"y11l3-plenary-2-a\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"plenary-2-a\" aria-label=\"Plenary 2 part a\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y11l3-plenary-2-b\">(b) State the first value output. [1]</label><input id=\"y11l3-plenary-2-b\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"plenary-2-b\" aria-label=\"Plenary 2 part b\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y11l3-plenary-2-c\">(c) State the last value output. [1]</label><input id=\"y11l3-plenary-2-c\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"plenary-2-c\" aria-label=\"Plenary 2 part c\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-actions\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"donow-btn\" id=\"y11l3-plenary-2-check\">Check answers</button><strong>Total: 3 marks</strong></div><div id=\"y11l3-plenary-2-feedback\" class=\"pseudocode-feedback\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"></div><p class=\"exam-source\">Practice question in the Cambridge IGCSE 0478 exam style.</p></div></div>"},{"id":"plenary-3","label":"Plenary: Trace a Counting Loop","type":"short-answer-validation","validatorId":"y11l3-plenary-3","validatorKey":"y11l3_plenary_3","content":"<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Plenary: Trace a Counting Loop</h2><p class=\"lesson-lead\">This loop is condition-controlled, like the WHILE loop from the extension, not count-controlled like today's FOR loop. Trace it exactly as written. The user enters 20 when prompted for Number.</p><div class=\"lesson-do-now-columns\"><div><div class=\"lesson-code\"><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">1&nbsp;&nbsp;Count &lt;- 0</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">2&nbsp;&nbsp;INPUT Number</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">3&nbsp;&nbsp;Value &lt;- Count * Number</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">4&nbsp;&nbsp;WHILE Value &lt;= 100</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">5&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Count &lt;- Count + 1</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">6&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Value &lt;- Count * Number</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">7&nbsp;&nbsp;ENDWHILE</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">8&nbsp;&nbsp;Count &lt;- Count - 1</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">9&nbsp;&nbsp;OUTPUT Count</div></div></div><div class=\"lesson-exam-card\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-responses\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y11l3-plenary-3-a\">(a) State the value of Count after the first pass through the loop body. [1]</label><input id=\"y11l3-plenary-3-a\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"plenary-3-a\" aria-label=\"Plenary 3 part a\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y11l3-plenary-3-b\">(b) State the value of Value the final time it is calculated, the one that stops the loop. [1]</label><input id=\"y11l3-plenary-3-b\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"plenary-3-b\" aria-label=\"Plenary 3 part b\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y11l3-plenary-3-c\">(c) State the value of Count after line 8 executes. [1]</label><input id=\"y11l3-plenary-3-c\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"plenary-3-c\" aria-label=\"Plenary 3 part c\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y11l3-plenary-3-d\">(d) State the output. [1]</label><input id=\"y11l3-plenary-3-d\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"plenary-3-d\" aria-label=\"Plenary 3 part d\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-actions\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"donow-btn\" id=\"y11l3-plenary-3-check\">Check answers</button><strong>Total: 4 marks</strong></div><div id=\"y11l3-plenary-3-feedback\" class=\"pseudocode-feedback\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"></div><p class=\"exam-source\">Algorithm adapted from Cambridge IGCSE 0478, October/November 2025 Paper 21, Question 7</p></div></div>"},{"id":"plenary-4","label":"Plenary: Same Loop, New Input","type":"short-answer-validation","validatorId":"y11l3-plenary-4","validatorKey":"y11l3_plenary_4","content":"<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Plenary: Same Loop, New Input</h2><p class=\"lesson-lead\">The same algorithm as the last slide, a different input. This time the user enters 110 when prompted for Number.</p><div class=\"lesson-do-now-columns\"><div><div class=\"lesson-code\"><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">1&nbsp;&nbsp;Count &lt;- 0</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">2&nbsp;&nbsp;INPUT Number</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">3&nbsp;&nbsp;Value &lt;- Count * Number</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">4&nbsp;&nbsp;WHILE Value &lt;= 100</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">5&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Count &lt;- Count + 1</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">6&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Value &lt;- Count * Number</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">7&nbsp;&nbsp;ENDWHILE</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">8&nbsp;&nbsp;Count &lt;- Count - 1</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">9&nbsp;&nbsp;OUTPUT Count</div></div></div><div class=\"lesson-exam-card\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-responses\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y11l3-plenary-4-a\">(a) State the value of Value calculated on line 3, before the loop is tested for the first time. [1]</label><input id=\"y11l3-plenary-4-a\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"plenary-4-a\" aria-label=\"Plenary 4 part a\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y11l3-plenary-4-b\">(b) State the value of Value calculated inside the loop, on line 6. [1]</label><input id=\"y11l3-plenary-4-b\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"plenary-4-b\" aria-label=\"Plenary 4 part b\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y11l3-plenary-4-c\">(c) State the output. [1]</label><input id=\"y11l3-plenary-4-c\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"plenary-4-c\" aria-label=\"Plenary 4 part c\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-actions\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"donow-btn\" id=\"y11l3-plenary-4-check\">Check answers</button><strong>Total: 3 marks</strong></div><div id=\"y11l3-plenary-4-feedback\" class=\"pseudocode-feedback\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"></div><p class=\"exam-source\">Algorithm adapted from Cambridge IGCSE 0478, October/November 2025 Paper 21, Question 7</p></div></div>"}],"validators":{"y11l3_do_now":[{"suffix":"a","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"^\\s*\"?b\"?\\s*$","flags":"i"},"feedback":"A score of 68 does not reach 70, but does it reach 60?"},{"suffix":"b","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"^\\s*\"?e\"?\\s*$","flags":"i"},"feedback":"A score of 35 does not reach 40, but does it reach 30?"},{"suffix":"c","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"^\\s*\"?f\"?\\s*$","flags":"i"},"feedback":"A score of 15 does not reach any of the listed boundaries."}],"y11l3_plenary":[{"suffix":"a","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"^\\s*3\\s*$","flags":""},"feedback":"Total after Number = 2: 0 + 1 + 2."},{"suffix":"b","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"^\\s*10\\s*$","flags":""},"feedback":"Total after Number = 4: keep adding through to 4."},{"suffix":"c","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"^\\s*4\\s*$","flags":""},"feedback":"FOR Number <- 1 TO 4 runs once for every value from 1 to 4 inclusive."},{"suffix":"d","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"^\\s*10\\s*$","flags":""},"feedback":"OUTPUT Total runs once, after the loop finishes."}],"y11l3_plenary_2":[{"suffix":"a","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"^\\s*4\\s*$","flags":""},"feedback":"FOR X <- 2 TO 5 runs once for every value from 2 to 5 inclusive."},{"suffix":"b","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"^\\s*2\\s*$","flags":""},"feedback":"The first pass uses the starting value of X."},{"suffix":"c","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"^\\s*5\\s*$","flags":""},"feedback":"The last pass uses the final value of X, right before the loop stops."}],"y11l3_plenary_3":[{"suffix":"a","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"^\\s*1\\s*$","flags":""},"feedback":"Count starts at 0. The first pass through the loop body adds 1 to it."},{"suffix":"b","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"^\\s*120\\s*$","flags":""},"feedback":"Keep multiplying Count (now 6) by 20. That value is the one greater than 100 that finally stops the loop."},{"suffix":"c","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"^\\s*5\\s*$","flags":""},"feedback":"Line 8 subtracts 1 from whatever Count reached right before the loop stopped."},{"suffix":"d","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"^\\s*5\\s*$","flags":""},"feedback":"OUTPUT Count runs once, after line 8."}],"y11l3_plenary_4":[{"suffix":"a","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"^\\s*0\\s*$","flags":""},"feedback":"Line 3 runs before the loop is tested for the first time, using Count's starting value of 0."},{"suffix":"b","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"^\\s*110\\s*$","flags":""},"feedback":"The loop body runs once: Count becomes 1, then line 6 recalculates Value using the new Count."},{"suffix":"c","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"^\\s*0\\s*$","flags":""},"feedback":"110 is already greater than 100, so the loop stops after only one pass. Line 8 then subtracts 1 from Count."}]},"pseudocodeValidators":{}}